{title: I Got My Foot On The Rock}
{key: A}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]I started out to [D]win this [A]race
[A]To serve the Lord and to [B]look upon his [E]face.
But the [A]way's been long and the [D]way's been rough,
But there is [A]one thing for [D]sure
I've got [E]my mind made [A]up.

{comment: Chorus}
[A]I've got my foot on the rock [D]and my mind's made [A]up.
[A]Tho I walk through the lonely valley
Tho I [B]drink from the bitter [E]cup
[A]When the devil comes a knocking
[D]Showing me an easier way.
[D]I stand right [A]square on my [D]feet
I throw my [A]head in the[D] air
I look him [A]straight in the[D] eye
I say my [A]foot's on the [D]rock and my [E]minds made [A]up.

{comment: Verse 2}
[A]Now the devil he will tempt you
And [D]fill your way with [A]strife.
[A]He'll make you sick in body even [B]try to take your [E]life.
But if you [A]put your trust in Jesus
[A]And say Lord [D]I've had enough
The Lord [A]will say move on [D]Satan
He's got [E]his mind made [A]up.

{comment: Verse 3}
[A]Now Job was a man who was [D]tempted in every [A]way,
[A]The devil took his family he lay [B]sick both night and [E]day.
[A]His wife she came a saying
Curse God - [D]you've had enough
He said you [A]talk like a foolish [D]woman
I've got my [E]mind made [A]up.
